To maintain this code properly, the following three repositories have to be
tracked for changes (maintenance details below):

- https://github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3
- https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher
- https://github.com/libtom/libtomcrypt


Update code from https://github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3
----------------------------------------------------

Current release: v1.14.52 (b0be46fa28d17ee0b65c79774ac0dad84b6db068)
Minimum Go version: 1.21

1. git clone mattn/go-sqlite3 new version to temp dir
2. Use ./track_go-sqlite3.sh <mattn/go-sqlite3 dir>
3. find & sed mattn/go-sqlite3 to sjzar/go-sqlcipher
4. rewrite pragma args golang code to sqlite3.go
5. Remove Go files deleted upstream (for this upgrade: sqlite3_go18.go,
   sqlite3_go18_test.go, sqlite3_go113_test.go; their code moved into other files).
6. Keep the default database/sql driver name "sqlcipher" in both cgo and
   non-cgo builds, and update the examples and tests to use that name.
7. Prefix all //export callback names and their Go/C references with gsc_.
   A C macro alone does not rename cgo's Go-side references to callback addresses.
8. Preserve flags.go and run go generate ./... to regenerate sqlcipher_namespace.h.
   The forced include applies to the SQLite API and C helpers in every C/cgo
   compilation unit. Do not suppress duplicate symbols at link time.
9. Run make test.

This procedure updates the Go driver, tests and examples only. The SQLCipher
amalgamation and LibTomCrypt retain the versions below; do not copy mattn's
sqlite3-binding.c/h over them. The bundled SQLCipher 4.12.0 engine is based on
SQLite 3.51.1, independent of mattn's bundled SQLite version.

Namespace header generation scans unpreprocessed declarations, so it includes
platform and optional APIs. A few omitted SQLite APIs become preprocessor
constants; the generator preserves their build-option guards. Update these
guards if a later engine upgrade changes those declarations.


Update code from https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher
-------------------------------------------------------

Current release: v4.12.0

Note:
v4.12.0 removed support for LibTomCrypt, the corresponding commit needs to be reverted. Related ISSUE: https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher/issues/564

Execute:
1. git clone sqlcipher to temp dir
2. git checkout v4.12.0 & git revert 3607cf6 (https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher/commit/3607cf6)
3. ./configure --with-tempstore=yes CFLAGS="-DSQLITE_HAS_CODEC -DSQLITE_EXTRA_INIT=sqlcipher_extra_init -DSQLITE_EXTRA_SHUTDOWN=sqlcipher_extra_shutdown -DSQLCIPHER_CRYPTO_LIBTOMCRYPT"
4. make
5. track sqlite3.c & sqlite3.h files
6. rewrite flags.go add CFLAGSs


